    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: GOLD membership tier for 3+ member households\n\nThe `membershipTier` was previously derived purely from an owner's own stored fields (`namesakeCount`, `email`). GOLD depends on the household member count, which the owner can't know by itself \u2014 so I followed the codebase's existing \"assigner\" pattern (like `NamesakeCounter`/`CustomerCodeAssigner`) to record the count at create time, then derive the tier on read.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`MembershipTier.java`** \u2014 added the `GOLD` enum constant.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a stored `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with accessor, and updated `getMembershipTier()` to return `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falling through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE rules.\n\n3. **`HouseholdSizeAssigner.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility component that, on create, records the household size: existing stored owners sharing the owner's `householdId`, plus one for the owner itself. An owner with no `householdId` is a single-member household (size 1).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 wired the new assigner into `addOwner`, invoked right after `HouseholdAssigner` resolves/back-fills the `householdId` and before the owner is saved, so the count reflects the household \"after this create.\"\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum and updated its description (this regenerates `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` so the mapper can serialize GOLD).\n\n6. **All four `schema.sql` files** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column. The tests run under the hsqldb profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so this column is required for persistence.\n\nThe flow works correctly for the shared-household case: members 1 and 2 record sizes 1 and 2 (not GOLD), and the third member \u2014 after `HouseholdAssigner` back-fills the shared `householdId` onto the first two \u2014 records size 3 and reads back as GOLD, exactly as the acceptance test asserts.\n\nThe JDBC repository path needed no changes: it uses `BeanPropertySqlParameterSource`/`BeanPropertyRowMapper`, which map `householdSize` \u2194 `household_size` automatically now that the column exists.",
